By the Prime Number Theorem (\cref{thm:prime-number-equiv}), there exist $N_1 \in \mathbb{N}, C, t > 0$ such that  egin{equation*}  iggl\lvert  rac{1}{N} \sum_{n = 0}^{N - 1} \Lambda(n) - 1  iggrvert \leqslant  rac{C}{e^{t\sqrt{\log N}}} \end{equation*} for all \(N \geqslant N_1\). Now, since $\displaystyle \lim_{N 	o \infty}  rac{N}{\log^{m+b} N} = \infty$, there exists $N_2 \in \mathbb{N}$ so that, for all \(N \geqslant N_2\), \[  rac{N}{\log^{m + b} N} \geqslant N_1. \] Further, it can be verified that  egin{equation*} \lim_{N 	o \infty}  rac{2C\log^{m + b} N}{e^{t \sqrt{\log  rac{N}{\log^{m + b} N}}}} = 0, \end{equation*} so we can find $N_3 \in \mathbb{N}$ such that, for all \(N \geqslant N_3\),  egin{equation*}  rac{2C\log^{m + b} N}{e^{t \sqrt{\log  rac{N}{\log^{m + b} N}}}} \leqslant  rac{1}{\log^m N}. \end{equation*} With the above in mind, suppose $N \geqslant \max\{N_2, N_3\}$ and let $k =  loor{\log^m N}$. Accordingly,  egin{align}  iggl\lvert  rac{1}{N} \sum_{n = 0}^{N - 1} \Lambda(n) \mathrm{e}\Bigl( rac{\xi}{N} n \Bigr)  iggrvert &\leqslant  iggl\lvert  rac{1}{N} \sum_{n = 0}^{N - 1} \Lambda(n) f_k\Bigl( rac{\xi}{N} n \Bigr)  iggrvert +  iggl\lvert  rac{1}{N} \sum_{n = 0}^{N - 1} \Lambda(n)  iggl(\mathrm{e}\Bigl( rac{\xi}{N} n \Bigr) - f_k\Bigl( rac{\xi}{N} n \Bigr) iggr) iggrvert 
onumber\ &\leqslant  iggl\lvert  rac{1}{N} \sum_{n = 0}^{N - 1} \Lambda(n) f_k\Bigl( rac{\xi}{N} n \Bigr)  iggrvert +  rac{2\pi}{kN} \sum_{n = 0}^{N - 1} \Lambda(n), \end{align} where $f_k \colon \mathbb{R} 	o \mathbb{C}$ is the function satisfying $f_k(x) = \mathrm{e} igl( loor{kx}/k  igr)$. \cref{eqn:from-N-big} holds for all $\xi \in [0, N - 1]$. Suppose \(r \in \mathbb{N}\) such that $1 \leqslant r \leqslant \log^b N$. Then,  egin{equation}  iggl\lvert  rac{1}{N} \sum_{n = 0}^{N - 1} \Lambda(n) f_k\Bigl( rac{rn}{N} \Bigr)  iggrvert =  iggl\lvert  rac{1}{N} \sum_{\xi = 0}^{rk - 1} \mathrm{e} iggl( rac{\xi}{k}  iggr) \; \cdot \; \smashoperator{\sum_{\mkern26mu  rac{\xi N}{rk} \leqslant n <  rac{(\xi + 1) N}{rk}}} \Lambda(n)  iggrvert. \end{equation} Further, for each $\xi = 0, 1, \ldots, rk - 1$,  egin{align*}  iggl\lvert  rac{1}{N} \; \cdot \; \smashoperator{\sum_{\mkern26mu  rac{\xi N}{rk} \leqslant n <  rac{(\xi + 1)N}{rk}}} \Lambda(n) -  rac{1}{rk}  iggrvert &= \Biggl\lvert  iggl( rac{ rac{\xi + 1}{rk}}{ rac{(\xi + 1)N}{rk}} \:\smashoperator{\sum_{\mkern14mu n <  rac{(\xi + 1)N}{{rk}}}} \Lambda(n) -  rac{\xi + 1}{rk}  iggr) -  iggl( rac{ rac{\xi}{rk}}{ rac{\xi N}{rk}} \:\smashoperator{\sum_{\, n <  rac{\xi N}{rk}}} \Lambda(n) -  rac{\xi}{rk}  iggr)\Biggrvert\ &\leqslant  rac{\xi + 1}{rk} \Biggl\lvert  rac{1}{ rac{(\xi + 1)N}{rk}} \:\smashoperator{\sum_{\mkern14mu n <  rac{(\xi + 1)N}{{rk}}}} \Lambda(n) - 1 \Biggrvert +  rac{\xi}{rk} \Biggl\lvert  rac{1}{ rac{\xi N}{rk}} \:\smashoperator{\sum_{\, n <  rac{\xi N}{rk}}} \Lambda(n) - 1 \Biggrvert\ &\leqslant  rac{2C}{e^{t\sqrt{\log  rac{\xi N}{rk}}}}, \end{align*} because if $\xi \geqslant 1$, then  egin{equation*}  rac{\xi N}{rk} \geqslant  rac{N}{\log^{m + b} N}\geqslant N_1. \end{equation*} Denote $\displaystyle a(\xi) =  rac{1}{N} \;\cdot\; \smashoperator{\sum_{\mkern26mu  rac{\xi N}{rk} \leqslant n <  rac{(\xi + 1)N}{rk}}} \Lambda(n) -  rac{1}{rk}$. We have  egin{align}  iggl\lvert  rac{1}{N} \sum_{\xi = 0}^{rk - 1} \mathrm{e} iggl( rac{\xi}{k}  iggr) \;\cdot\; \smashoperator{\sum_{\mkern26mu  rac{\xi N}{rk} \leqslant n <  rac{(\xi + 1)N}{rk}}} \Lambda(n)  iggrvert &= \Biggl\lvert \sum_{\xi = 0}^{rk - 1} \mathrm{e} iggl( rac{\xi}{k}  iggr)  iggl( rac{1}{rk} + a(\xi)  iggr) \Biggrvert 
onumber\ &= \Biggl\lvert \sum_{\xi = 0}^{rk - 1} \mathrm{e} iggl( rac{\xi}{k}  iggr) a(\xi) \Biggrvert 
onumber\ &\leqslant  rac{2Crk}{e^{t\sqrt{\log  rac{N}{rk}}}} 
onumber\ &\leqslant  rac{2C\log^{m + b} N}{e^{t \sqrt{\log  rac{N}{\log^{m + b} N}}}} 
onumber\ &\leqslant  rac{1}{\log^m N}, \end{align} where the final inequality holds because $N \geqslant N_3$. By \cref{eqn:from-N-big}, \cref{eqn:restricting-xi}, and \cref{eqn:bounding-restricted-xi}, we obtain that, for any $\xi \in [1, \log^b N]$,  egin{align*}  iggl\lvert  rac{1}{N} \sum_{n = 0}^{N - 1} \Lambda(n) \mathrm{e} iggl( rac{\xi}{N} n  iggr)  iggrvert &\leqslant  rac{1}{\log^m N} +  rac{2\pi}{kN} \sum_{n = 0}^{N - 1} \Lambda(n).\ \intertext{Therefore, for all \(N \geqslant \max\{N_2, N_3\}\),} \sup_{1 \leqslant \xi \leqslant \log^b N}  iggl\lvert  rac{1}{N} \sum_{n = 0}^{N - 1} \Lambda(n) \mathrm{e} iggl( rac{\xi}{N} n  iggr)  iggrvert &\leqslant  rac{1}{\log^m N} +  rac{2\pi}{kN} \sum_{n = 0}^{N - 1} \Lambda(n).\ \intertext{So,} \sup_{1\leqslant \xi \leqslant \log^b N}  iggl\lvert  rac{1}{N} \sum_{n = 0}^{N - 1} \Lambda(n) \mathrm{e} iggl( rac{\xi}{N} n  iggr)  iggrvert &= {m O}  iggl( rac{1}{\log^m N}  iggr), \end{align*} as desired.

